CL 1
-- Named timer mutations emit their actual durable measurement over timer.changed;
-- the timer strip acknowledges only after its real visible label is committed (or a stopped timer disappears).
-- The periodic list refresh remains reconciliation; event delivery alone never counts as a visual ACK.
-- MODREL UI delivery contract: a mod UI intent needs an open command-bus socket and a
-- Readiness accepts a mounted heartbeat received after the request or the runtime probe ACK,
-- with one probe retry in the existing 1.5 s bound; cached heartbeats cannot authorize a closed page.
-- Consecutive completed commands reuse admission metadata only while the catalog stamp matches;
-- Authenticated mod bootstrap grounds the common theme/app/pane/timer metadata before the first action;
-- preparation never executes any procedure or UI mutation.
-- their goals, observer bindings and action identities remain fresh. File panes report committed text immediately.
-- fresh mounted shell plus its authenticated client/runtime readiness ACK (1.5s maximum)
-- before cold CL loading or durable mutation. A closed page refuses
-- immediately with nothing queued. Ten real agent theme/pane/timer actions must apply
-- and acknowledge within 2 seconds on normal storage; report loaded and idle timings.
-- Source routing hints only select manuals. Selected source/artifact/schema/effect
-- checks remain mandatory when the global compiled owner index has drifted.
-- Impact enrichment checks literal candidates before regex boundaries, avoiding
-- global interpreter stalls. Pane effects wait at most 2 seconds for their real
-- authenticated content ACK; timeout never counts as mounted content evidence.
L neyvia v1 -- Authored executable manual
